-I don't care.

781
00:27:03,090 --> 00:27:04,810
Let's see if we can
 get some directions.

782
00:27:04,810 --> 00:27:06,300
-Maybe it's Brigadoon.

783
00:27:06,300 --> 00:27:07,360
-There's someone at the door.

784
00:27:07,360 --> 00:27:07,860
-The hell?

785
00:27:11,300 --> 00:27:12,410
-Uh, you're rolling.

786
00:27:12,410 --> 00:27:14,590
Mister--

787
00:27:14,590 --> 00:27:16,610
-You know, every
 frame of this movie

788
00:27:16,610 --> 00:27:18,430
looks like someone's
 last known photograph.

789
00:27:21,430 --> 00:27:24,060
-On second thought, let's
 go back and ask him.

790
00:27:24,060 --> 00:27:25,740
I'm lost.

791
00:27:25,740 --> 00:27:29,150
-Shot on location in
 Spooner, Wisconsin.

792
00:27:29,150 --> 00:27:32,410
-Uh, are you part of
 the movie we're in?

793
00:27:32,410 --> 00:27:35,290
-I wet 'em!

794
00:27:35,290 --> 00:27:37,540
-Guy looks like a
 chainsaw sculpture.

795
00:27:37,540 --> 00:27:41,060
-Tom Cruise is Dr. John.

796
00:27:41,060 --> 00:27:44,480
-He seems tame enough.

797
00:27:44,480 --> 00:27:48,480
-Hey, you're nothin'
 special, either, you guys.

798
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:50,950
-Um, could somebody
 break the ice, please?

799
00:27:53,610 --> 00:27:55,150
-Well, this does look inviting.

800
00:27:58,920 --> 00:28:00,150
-Uh-- honey.

801
00:28:00,150 --> 00:28:01,540
Why don't you talk
 to the hairy man?

802
00:28:01,540 --> 00:28:02,960
You're good with people.

803
00:28:02,960 --> 00:28:04,450
There's a good girl.

804
00:28:04,450 --> 00:28:06,350
-Uh, you two stay
 with the nice man.

805
00:28:06,350 --> 00:28:07,570
I'm going to go find a Ramada.

806
00:28:11,330 --> 00:28:12,780
-OK, we brought the kid.

807
00:28:12,780 --> 00:28:14,410
Now give us the negatives.

808
00:28:14,410 --> 00:28:17,740
-Oo, buh, I don't feel so good.

809
00:28:17,740 --> 00:28:18,750
Bluh.

810
00:28:18,750 --> 00:28:20,250
-I am Torgo.

811
00:28:20,250 --> 00:28:22,890
I take care of the place
 while the Master is away.

812
00:28:22,890 --> 00:28:23,770
-The Master?

813
00:28:23,770 --> 00:28:25,200
Bobby Fischer?

814
00:28:25,200 --> 00:28:28,750
-How proud your parents must be.

815
00:28:28,750 --> 00:28:29,710
-But the child.

816
00:28:29,710 --> 00:28:32,120
I'm not sure the
 Master would approve.

817
00:28:32,120 --> 00:28:33,570
Or the dog.

818
00:28:33,570 --> 00:28:35,430
The Master doesn't
 like children.

819
00:28:35,430 --> 00:28:36,590
-Hey, he's W.C. Fields.

820
00:28:36,590 --> 00:28:38,810
-We only want to know
 where Valley Lodge is.

821
00:28:38,810 --> 00:28:39,610
-Which way do we go?

822
00:28:42,180 --> 00:28:43,940
-There is no place
 like that around here.

823
00:28:49,520 --> 00:28:50,020
[BELCHES]

824
00:28:50,020 --> 00:28:51,050
-Oh, there, better.

825
00:28:51,050 --> 00:28:51,950
Ahem.

826
00:28:51,950 --> 00:28:52,860
Ahh.

827
00:28:52,860 --> 00:28:53,630
-Mike, I'm scared.

828
00:28:53,630 --> 00:28:55,280
-Of what?

829
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:56,790
-It's getting dark.

830
00:28:56,790 --> 00:28:58,510
-Sure, he is from
 the edge of Hell.

831
00:28:58,510 --> 00:29:00,510
-Which way is out of here?

832
00:29:00,510 --> 00:29:02,440
-Look, lady, I have
 that effect on people,

833
00:29:02,440 --> 00:29:04,170
but I'm not a bad guy.

834
00:29:04,170 --> 00:29:05,950
-There is no way out here.

835
00:29:05,950 --> 00:29:08,030
It will be dark soon.

836
00:29:08,030 --> 00:29:09,320
There is no way out of here.

837
00:29:09,320 --> 00:29:10,410
-It'll be dark soon.

838
00:29:10,410 --> 00:29:11,450
-No way out?

839
00:29:14,180 --> 00:29:16,620
-Well, you know, we, we could
 spend the night here and then

840
00:29:16,620 --> 00:29:17,810
tomorrow--

841
00:29:17,810 --> 00:29:19,570
-I-I don't want to
 spend the night here.

842
00:29:19,570 --> 00:29:21,180
I don't like the
 look of the place.

843
00:29:21,180 --> 00:29:22,610
-Well, it seems we
 have no alternative.

844
00:29:22,610 --> 00:29:24,000
Well, how about it, Torgo?

845
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:25,740
Can we spend the night here?

846
00:29:25,740 --> 00:29:27,810
-Look, we got a convention
 in town, I'm sorry.

847
00:29:27,810 --> 00:29:30,740
-I don't know what
 else we can do.

848
00:29:30,740 --> 00:29:33,330
-Mike, I don't
 want to stay here.

849
00:29:33,330 --> 00:29:36,400
-A-and the Master
 wouldn't approve.

850
00:29:36,400 --> 00:29:37,400
-Don't worry about it.

851
00:29:37,400 --> 00:29:40,760
We're here now, and I'm sure
 the master won't throw us out.

852
00:29:40,760 --> 00:29:41,920
Well?

853
00:29:41,920 --> 00:29:43,400
How about it, Torgo?

854
00:29:43,400 --> 00:29:45,490
-I don't want to
 stay, let's leave.

855
00:29:45,490 --> 00:29:47,710
-The guy buys right into
 the whole Master thing.

856
00:29:47,710 --> 00:29:49,560
-I don't know about it.

857
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:50,510
I just don't know.

858
00:29:50,510 --> 00:29:52,570
-I'll have to run it
 by my sales manager.

859
00:29:55,650 --> 00:29:59,680
-And the negotiations
 continued into the night.

860
00:29:59,680 --> 00:30:01,090
-Ambiguity is scary.

861
00:30:04,850 --> 00:30:06,260
-Boy, I'm torn.

862
00:30:06,260 --> 00:30:06,760
Torgo?

863
00:30:06,760 --> 00:30:08,540
My wife?

864
00:30:08,540 --> 00:30:10,470
Hmmm.

865
00:30:10,470 --> 00:30:11,680
-What is this, Final Jeopardy?

866
00:30:14,620 --> 00:30:15,120
-Now, look.

867
00:30:15,120 --> 00:30:19,890
I've got some beans
 going back there, I--

868
00:30:19,890 --> 00:30:22,210
-The rod of my
 staff discomfort me.

869
00:30:22,210 --> 00:30:25,050
-He's the guy you used to know
 who works at a Kinney's Shoes

870
00:30:25,050 --> 00:30:27,880
and won't leave you alone.

871
00:30:27,880 --> 00:30:29,320
-Man, pillow pants.

872
00:30:33,840 --> 00:30:35,900
-You can vacation
 with Torgo but don't

873
00:30:35,900 --> 00:30:37,960
bring your American
 Express card.

874
00:30:37,960 --> 00:30:38,860
-Very well.

875
00:30:38,860 --> 00:30:41,410
The Master will
 be very disturbed.

876
00:30:41,410 --> 00:30:44,440
-Here, go chat with the
 Master, honey, there.

877
00:30:44,440 --> 00:30:46,150
-Heh, heh, kids.

878
00:30:46,150 --> 00:30:46,880
You got family, Torgo?

879
00:30:46,880 --> 00:30:49,560
-I'll get the luggage.

880
00:30:49,560 --> 00:30:53,790
-Uhh-- that's not how you
 wear your Depends, Torgo.

881
00:30:53,790 --> 00:30:55,220
-Been hittin' the
 Thighmaster, Torgo?

882
00:31:00,590 --> 00:31:02,580
-Torgo, we'll stay tonight
 and then tomorrow--

883
00:31:02,580 --> 00:31:03,850
-You must leave.

884
00:31:03,850 --> 00:31:05,680
You cannot stay.

885
00:31:05,680 --> 00:31:08,310
The Master would
 not, uh, approve.

886
00:31:08,310 --> 00:31:10,910
-Oh, what does the
 Master approve?

887
00:31:10,910 --> 00:31:11,850
-Uh.

888
00:31:11,850 --> 00:31:13,270
Heh.

889
00:31:13,270 --> 00:31:16,390
Uh, the door's over
 that way, Torgo.

890
00:31:16,390 --> 00:31:17,880
-I'm losing it.

891
00:31:17,880 --> 00:31:20,110
Left-- oh, there I go,
 I'm going left, help.

892
00:31:20,110 --> 00:31:21,320
I'm-- oh, ohh.

893
00:31:21,320 --> 00:31:24,950
-It's like having Joe
 Cocker as your bellhop.

894
00:31:24,950 --> 00:31:27,610
-Uh, careful, honey, Torgo's
 been marking his territory.

895
00:31:32,180 --> 00:31:33,600
-Oh, look, honey.

896
00:31:33,600 --> 00:31:35,110
Torgo has a little
 altar to Ba'al.

897
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:41,230
-Looks like they had a little
 problem with the last fire

898
00:31:41,230 --> 00:31:42,190
there.

899
00:31:42,190 --> 00:31:43,670
Yule log got out of hand.

900
00:31:48,810 --> 00:31:50,650
-See, you're feeling
 better already.

901
00:31:50,650 --> 00:31:54,960
-Rolling in filth
 will do that for you.

902
00:31:54,960 --> 00:31:55,950
-Look at this.

903
00:32:03,850 --> 00:32:04,840
-What the--?

904
00:32:04,840 --> 00:32:06,820
What-- oh.

905
00:32:06,820 --> 00:32:11,610
-The haunting "Torgo Theme."

906
00:32:11,610 --> 00:32:12,890
-Well, it's almost
 as if you don't

907
00:32:12,890 --> 00:32:14,780
want him to carry
 your luggage, dear.

908
00:32:14,780 --> 00:32:15,820
-Hey, Torgo, gotta match?

909
00:32:15,820 --> 00:32:17,260
Heh, just kidding.

910
00:32:17,260 --> 00:32:21,190
-I swear I know that guy.

911
00:32:21,190 --> 00:32:21,900
-Heh, it's fun.

912
00:32:21,900 --> 00:32:23,970
Heh, fun.

913
00:32:23,970 --> 00:32:26,960
-Never seen her so happy, dear.

914
00:32:26,960 --> 00:32:28,230
-I'm bemused by this
 plucky painting.

915
00:32:30,920 --> 00:32:34,990
-It's a, uh, Frank Frazetta
 of a, uh, of Frank Zappa.

916
00:32:34,990 --> 00:32:39,920
-I'm thinking of having that
 tattooed on my face, dearest.

917
00:32:39,920 --> 00:32:44,170
-Tonight, on "Night Gallery."

918
00:32:44,170 --> 00:32:46,740
-OK, so, should we
 head down to the bar?

919
00:32:46,740 --> 00:32:48,720
-Must be the Master, himself.

920
00:32:48,720 --> 00:32:50,880
-Yeah, he just exudes
 authority, he does.

921
00:32:50,880 --> 00:32:53,110
MARGARET (OFFSCREEN):
 Oh, Mike, I'm scared.

922
00:32:53,110 --> 00:32:54,530
He has the meanest look.

923
00:32:54,530 --> 00:32:56,790
-Yeah, and it won't go
 with your sofa, either.

924
00:32:56,790 --> 00:32:59,010
MIKE (OFFSCREEN): I'd hate
 to run up on him in the dark,

925
00:32:59,010 --> 00:33:00,920
or even in the light,
 for that matter.

926
00:33:00,920 --> 00:33:03,060
-Honey, uh, should we
 be in a cut away here?

927
00:33:03,060 --> 00:33:05,180
-Um-- next slide, please.

928
00:33:05,180 --> 00:33:07,180
Next slide.

929
00:33:07,180 --> 00:33:10,130
-Hey, look at those lamprey
 eels on the wall back there.

930
00:33:12,910 --> 00:33:15,130
-I left a piece of chewed
 gum on your pillow.

931
00:33:19,380 --> 00:33:22,240
-Oh, that's the playful
 side of Torgo, right there.

932
00:33:22,240 --> 00:33:23,780
He has fun.

933
00:33:23,780 --> 00:33:27,020
-He's the clown that makes the
 dark side fun. (SINGING) Torgo.

934
00:33:27,020 --> 00:33:29,400
-Uh, the dog is
 sharp again, Mommy.

935
00:33:29,400 --> 00:33:29,900
See?

936
00:33:32,880 --> 00:33:33,740
That must be your Master.

937
00:33:33,740 --> 00:33:35,930
Where did you say he was?

938
00:33:35,930 --> 00:33:38,760
-He's in Houston this week.

939
00:33:38,760 --> 00:33:40,180
-But he is with us always.

940
00:33:40,180 --> 00:33:42,130
No matter where we
 go, he is with us.

941
00:33:42,130 --> 00:33:44,290
-You know, I bet the Master
 and I would really get along.

942
00:33:44,290 --> 00:33:45,340
I'd like to think that.

943
00:33:45,340 --> 00:33:46,310
-What?

944
00:33:46,310 --> 00:33:48,230
-No matter where he goes?

945
00:33:48,230 --> 00:33:50,310
What does that mean?

946
00:33:50,310 --> 00:33:51,490
And that dog.

947
00:33:51,490 --> 00:33:54,090
It's the most vicious-looking
 animal I've ever seen.

948
00:33:54,090 --> 00:33:57,100
-Well, I, hope he goes
 where the Master goes.

949
00:33:57,100 --> 00:33:59,460
-There is nothing
 to fear, madam.

950
00:33:59,460 --> 00:34:01,360
The Master likes you.

951
00:34:01,360 --> 00:34:02,950
Nothing will happen to you.

952
00:34:02,950 --> 00:34:04,840
He likes you.

953
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:06,260
-Likes me?

954
00:34:06,260 --> 00:34:08,460
I thought you said he was dead.

955
00:34:08,460 --> 00:34:08,960
-Honey!

956
00:34:08,960 --> 00:34:11,050
You're embarrassing Torgo.

957
00:34:11,050 --> 00:34:11,870
-Dead?

958
00:34:11,870 --> 00:34:14,130
No, madam, not dead
 the way you know it.

959
00:34:14,130 --> 00:34:16,160
-Uh, look, it's
 kinda complicated.

960
00:34:16,160 --> 00:34:19,630
But I can show you to your room.

961
00:34:19,630 --> 00:34:21,880
-Not dead the way you know it.

962
00:34:21,880 --> 00:34:24,740
He is with us always.

963
00:34:24,740 --> 00:34:26,190
-Makes sense to me, honey.

964
00:34:26,190 --> 00:34:27,260
What's your problem?

965
00:34:27,260 --> 00:34:29,210
-Mike, I don't like this.

966
00:34:29,210 --> 00:34:30,110
-Nothing to worry about.

967
00:34:30,110 --> 00:34:33,080
It's only your imagination.

968
00:34:33,080 --> 00:34:34,460
-Can Scruffy eat
 this silverfish?

969
00:34:38,830 --> 00:34:39,540
-Well, then.

970
00:34:39,540 --> 00:34:44,930
So, Master, uh, pay
 ya pretty well, huh?

971
00:34:44,930 --> 00:34:46,010
-Man, that poor kid.

972
00:34:46,010 --> 00:34:46,510
-Mhm.

973
00:34:46,510 --> 00:34:47,430
-Gee.

974
00:34:47,430 --> 00:34:51,870
-I think that it's best that I
 show you to the bedrooms now.

975
00:34:51,870 --> 00:34:53,390
-Oh, you'd like
 that, wouldn't you?

976
00:34:57,980 --> 00:34:58,480
-Hmm.

977
00:34:58,480 --> 00:34:59,490
Nice guy.

978
00:34:59,490 --> 00:35:00,430
[HOWLING]

979
00:35:00,430 --> 00:35:01,260
-Oh my God!

980
00:35:01,260 --> 00:35:02,850
Mike, what was that?

981
00:35:02,850 --> 00:35:04,350
-It's Howlin' Wolf.
 (SINGING) Gonna

982
00:35:04,350 --> 00:35:07,370
womp that wang dang
 doodle all night long.

983
00:35:14,580 --> 00:35:16,000
[HOWLING]

984
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,670
-Hey, look, I know you're
 an evil hell beast,

985
00:35:18,670 --> 00:35:19,570
but could you hold it down?

986
00:35:19,570 --> 00:35:21,090
It's after nine and we got kids!

987
00:35:21,090 --> 00:35:22,740
-I'll go check this out.

988
00:35:22,740 --> 00:35:23,240
Haha!

989
00:35:23,240 --> 00:35:23,920
Fifi to the rescue!

990
00:35:23,920 --> 00:35:26,300
[BARKING]

991
00:35:26,300 --> 00:35:26,920
-That's it.

992
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:27,610
Mix it up, Fifi.

993
00:35:27,610 --> 00:35:28,110
Go.

994
00:35:28,110 --> 00:35:28,610
Go.

995
00:35:28,610 --> 00:35:29,580
Go neck, Fifi.

996
00:35:29,580 --> 00:35:31,540
Neck.

997
00:35:31,540 --> 00:35:32,520
-What happened?

998
00:35:32,520 --> 00:35:33,490
I heard--

999
00:35:33,490 --> 00:35:33,990
-Stay here.

1000
00:35:33,990 --> 00:35:35,230
Get back into the house.

1001
00:35:35,230 --> 00:35:36,460
-Someone left a cake
 out in the rain.

1002
00:35:39,240 --> 00:35:43,360
-Sounds like Gene
 Krupa's out here.

1003
00:35:43,360 --> 00:35:44,560
-OK, let's see here.

1004
00:35:44,560 --> 00:35:48,170
Wet naps, flashlight,
 revolver, good.

1005
00:35:48,170 --> 00:35:50,480
-Finally, my chance to
 get rid of that damn dog.

1006
00:35:53,330 --> 00:35:56,630
-Ugh, look at the pile he left.

1007
00:35:56,630 --> 00:35:58,190
-Petrified poodle.

1008
00:36:01,720 --> 00:36:02,550
-Uh, good news honey.

1009
00:36:02,550 --> 00:36:03,570
We can get that Rottweiler.

1010
00:36:03,570 --> 00:36:05,760
-Get back in the house, damn it!

1011
00:36:05,760 --> 00:36:06,630
-My God, Mike.

1012
00:36:06,630 --> 00:36:07,130
What happened?

1013
00:36:07,130 --> 00:36:08,250
-He's dead.

1014
00:36:08,250 --> 00:36:09,010
Peppy's been killed.

1015
00:36:09,010 --> 00:36:09,990
[GASPS]

1016
00:36:09,990 --> 00:36:10,960
-But who's Peppy?

1017
00:36:10,960 --> 00:36:11,940
-Get in the house, honey.

1018
00:36:11,940 --> 00:36:14,900
-Mike, what kind
 of place is this?

1019
00:36:14,900 --> 00:36:17,250
My God, what kind
 of place is this?

1020
00:36:17,250 --> 00:36:19,140
-I'll take care of everything.

1021
00:36:19,140 --> 00:36:20,110
Honey, get back in the house.

1022
00:36:24,000 --> 00:36:25,690
-Oh, and don't slam-- bang!

1023
00:36:25,690 --> 00:36:26,880
--the screen door.

1024
00:36:29,930 --> 00:36:30,920
-Come on, fling her.

1025
00:36:30,920 --> 00:36:33,550
Side arm, go for distance, woo!

1026
00:36:33,550 --> 00:36:34,540
Sorry, Fluffy.

1027
00:36:37,530 --> 00:36:39,200
-Well, I don't know
 what she got into,

1028
00:36:39,200 --> 00:36:41,090
but she's been out
 cold for hour-- oh.

1029
00:36:44,090 --> 00:36:47,310
-Uh, hi, dear the dog's dea--
 oh, that came out all wrong.

1030
00:36:51,400 --> 00:36:52,370
-Mike.

1031
00:36:52,370 --> 00:36:54,560
Oh, Mike, what could've done it?

1032
00:36:54,560 --> 00:36:56,610
-Ozzy Osbourne?

1033
00:36:56,610 --> 00:36:58,300
-What are you guys
 talking about?

1034
00:36:58,300 --> 00:36:59,570
Where's my dog?

1035
00:36:59,570 --> 00:37:02,140
-Honey, it was probably
 some animal from the desert.

1036
00:37:02,140 --> 00:37:03,660
This place must be full of them.

1037
00:37:03,660 --> 00:37:05,570
-Are you talk--
 talking about my dog?

1038
00:37:05,570 --> 00:37:07,690
Where's my dog?

1039
00:37:07,690 --> 00:37:08,270
-Peppy?

